WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.090
Speaker 1: So let's now get from strategy
and approach.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.559
To Tactics.

00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:11.519
I got a really interesting email from Eric
and Colleen, I think Eric and Colleen are

00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:18.210
a couple that watch the show, and what Eric
and Colleen wrote to me about was the new

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:19.880
democratic talking points.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:25.460
They seem to understand that Democrats have
been falling to Republicans in many cases

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:31.410
because Republicans much more effectively
play on fear and anger, and that Republican

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.770
talking points just naturally lend themselves
more to that.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:39.140
And Eric and Colleen wrote to me and said,
David, you know, if you if we want to develop

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.480
on the left the same motivating fear and anger
that the Republican Party does.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.910
We need to change our messaging.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:51.390
Now, Eric and Colleen say it doesn't even
matter if our messaging is true.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.560
Republicans lie all the time.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.170
So my question to you as I go through these
possible talking points that Eric and Colleen

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:04.600
suggested is how do we feel about using talking
points that we know in some cases aren't true?

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.909
Is that taking the low road and we don't want
to do it, but here are the new talking points

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:15.990
that Eric and Colleen suggest should be repeated
and repeated and repeated in 2022 and 2024

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.159
on abortion.

00:01:17.159 --> 00:01:20.619
Okay, these are hypothetical talking points
on abortion.

00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:26.880
Republicans want to force you to have babies
and they will create a dangerous and expensive

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.429
black market of back alley abortions.

00:01:29.429 --> 00:01:35.830
It's not really an exaggeration, actually,
it's using maybe hyperbolic language, but

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:39.720
that one isn't wrong on guns.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:46.240
Republicans will make it so easy to get guns
that every criminal will be armed, and many

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:53.140
of those will be armed with semi-automatic
outfitted with high-capacity magazines.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.439
Every criminal will be armed.

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:59.100
It's an exaggeration, but certainly the right
wants to make it really easy to get guns on

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.630
immigration.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.189
Republicans will shut down the borders.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:07.950
Women and children who are fleeing violence
are going to die at the border of disease

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:13.310
and starvation or be sent back to death in
their home countries.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:18.770
Tipper Bolick But it plays on fear and it
plays on anger education.

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:24.020
Republicans will take control away from school
boards and implement a federal government

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.420
curriculum.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.240
It won't be based on science.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.090
It won't be based in accurate historical realities.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:35.880
It's going to be alternative facts, lies and
Christianity, and they will impose it on your

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.880
children.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:43.230
OK, on the pandemic, Republicans will not
allow enforcement of any safety measure.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:47.380
They will ban mask requirements, they will
ban vaccine requirements, and they are going

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.350
to allow this or a future pandemic to run
rampant.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:57.010
They will allow innocent Americans to keep
dying just to avoid implementing any regulations

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.700
on deregulation.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:04.420
Republicans are going to let poison and sewage
pour into our water systems.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:10.020
They're going to build more fossil fuel plants
near your homes, and there will be more respiratory

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:15.010
disease and cancer as a result on inequality.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:19.730
Republicans will allow wealth concentration
to deepen, and it will destroy the middle

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:20.730
class.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:24.120
That one seems just pretty, pretty sober,
actually.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:30.040
On taxes, Republicans will continue to allow
the rich and corporations to get away with

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.580
paying no taxes or close to it.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.850
The rich will get richer, concentration of
power will become worse, and it will crush

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:37.850
the middle class.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:42.250
And lastly, on infrastructure, the talking
point proposed by Eric and Colleen is our

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:46.990
infrastructure, roads, electrical grid, military
educational system.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:53.350
It will be bankrupt thanks to the rich and
corporations paying almost no taxes.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:58.330
This is more hyperbolic language than Democrats
and the Left tend to use.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:02.380
It's mostly accurate with some exaggerations.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.530
How do you feel about it?

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:13.510
Are these do Democrats and does the left need
to find talking points to generate that exact

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:18.269
same type of fear and anger that the right
does without and out lies?

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:22.099
And if the answer is yes, the left needs to
do that.

00:04:22.099 --> 00:04:27.919
Does the left need to do it without exaggeration
and without hyperbole?

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:32.139
Or is it OK to do it the way Eric and Colleen
are suggesting?

00:04:32.139 --> 00:04:33.169
Let me know your thoughts.

00:04:33.169 --> 00:04:36.530
Let me know what talking points you think
the left should adopt.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:39.760
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman
and we'll be back with more right after this.

